IMPORT prelude

-- National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR); no
-- daydate import. Dates are compared by serial.
--
-- "At least 4 months before the day the person turns 18" and "at least 3 months, but not more than 6 months, before that
-- day" (Rules s 15(2)) are measured to the same day-number in the earlier month, or the last day of that month where it
-- has no such day (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the National Redress Scheme Rules 2018`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date` a `falls after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date` a `falls before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date` a `falls on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date` a `falls on or after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL b

-- The number of days in a calendar month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of year` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- A running count of months (years times 12, plus the month less one), so that months can be added and taken away.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the running month of` d MEANS (DATE_YEAR d TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1)

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of running month` c MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 12)

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of running month` c MEANS (c MINUS (`the year of running month` c TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- The day with the same day-number n months on from d (n may be negative); where that month has no such day, its last day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the matching day` n `months from` d MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY d AT MOST `the days in month` `rm` `of year` `ry`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY d) `rm` `ry`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the days in month` `rm` `of year` `ry`) `rm` `ry`
    WHERE
        `rc` MEANS `the running month of` d PLUS n
        `rm` MEANS `the month of running month` `rc`
        `ry` MEANS `the year of running month` `rc`

-- The day a person turns 18: the 18th anniversary of their birth. A person born on 29 February turns 18 on 1 March in a
-- year with no 29 February (fork F3).
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the eighteenth birthday for` `the date of birth` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the date of birth` EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY `the date of birth` EQUALS 29 AND `the days in month` 2 `of year` (DATE_YEAR `the date of birth` PLUS 18) EQUALS 28
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 (DATE_YEAR `the date of birth` PLUS 18)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the date of birth`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of birth`) (DATE_YEAR `the date of birth` PLUS 18)

-- Act s 193(1)(a): the scheme sunset day is the tenth anniversary of the scheme start day (1 July 2018), unless the rules
-- prescribe a later day; the deposited Rules (Compilation No. 9) prescribe none. Rules s 15(1) uses the term.
`the sunset day of the scheme` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2028
